From 8517120826d8a308a796d8e1cf6b96d7ee108812 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bianca Giocas <bgiocas@arista.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:17:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: aspeed: limit Aristabmc U-Boot relocation

Aristabmc DRAM starts at 0x400000000. MAC0 ping succeeds when both the
descriptor rings and packet buffers are below 0x4f0000000, which is 3.75
GiB above that base. Splitting the allocations across the boundary fails:
low rings with buffers at 0x4f0000000 fail ARP, while rings at that address
with low buffers time out during TX. Moving both allocations below the
boundary restores ping. Tests show that both descriptor and packet DMA
accesses need the low DDR range.

Override board_get_usable_ram_top() to keep U-Boot relocation, the stack
and malloc heap below the tested boundary. The existing Ethernet driver
then allocates its rings and packet buffers in low DDR. Keep the detected
RAM size and DRAM banks unchanged so Linux retains the full memory range.
This does not constrain all LMB allocations or explicit physical addresses.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate
Signed-off-by: Bianca Giocas <bgiocas@arista.com>
---
 arch/arm/mach-aspeed/ast2700/board_common.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-aspeed/ast2700/board_common.c b/arch/arm/mach-aspeed/ast2700/board_common.c
index 6e25e5e9a4..f3c0010f41 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-aspeed/ast2700/board_common.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-aspeed/ast2700/board_common.c
@@ -46,6 +46,12 @@ int dram_init(void)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+phys_addr_t board_get_usable_ram_top(phys_size_t total_size)
+{
+	return min_t(phys_addr_t, gd->ram_top,
+		     gd->ram_base + 0xf0000000ULL);
+}
+
 #ifdef CONFIG_USB_GADGET_DOWNLOAD
 int g_dnl_get_board_bcd_device_number(int gcnum)
 {
